From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:16:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/data-control: Pass the receive fd straight to Wayland
 sources

When the selection is owned by a Wayland data source, hand the fd from
zwlr_data_control_offer_v1.receive directly to that source instead of
going through meta_selection_transfer_async() and a second pipe. This
is what wlroots does, and it saves a copy.

wl-clip-persist depends on it: after it takes over the selection it
reads its own offer back, and it recognizes that read as its own only
when its source's send event carries the pipe it passed to receive.
With the intermediate pipe it took every one of its own selections for
a new one and re-set the selection in a loop (about 17000 times in 8
seconds).

Owners that are not Wayland sources, such as the clipboard manager's
saved copy, still go through meta_selection_transfer_async().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland-private.h |  2 ++
 src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland.c         |  6 ++++++
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-data-control.c             | 13 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland-private.h b/src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland-private.h
index 82a9c52..50f5638 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland-private.h
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland-private.h
@@ -33,3 +33,5 @@ G_DECLARE_FINAL_TYPE (MetaSelectionSourceWayland,
 
 MetaSelectionSource * meta_selection_source_wayland_new (MetaWaylandDataSource *source);
 
+MetaWaylandDataSource * meta_selection_source_wayland_get_data_source (MetaSelectionSourceWayland *source_wayland);
+
diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland.c b/src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland.c
index 829272a..a650ea5 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland.c
@@ -166,3 +166,9 @@ meta_selection_source_wayland_new (MetaWaylandDataSource *data_source)
 
   return META_SELECTION_SOURCE (source_wayland);
 }
+
+MetaWaylandDataSource *
+meta_selection_source_wayland_get_data_source (MetaSelectionSourceWayland *source_wayland)
+{
+  return source_wayland->data_source;
+}
diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-data-control.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-data-control.c
index 1dd8f9b..84fc398 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-data-control.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-data-control.c
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 #include "core/display-private.h"
 #include "core/meta-selection-private.h"
 #include "meta/meta-selection-source-memory.h"
+#include "wayland/meta-selection-source-wayland-private.h"
 #include "wayland/meta-wayland-data-control.h"
 #include "wayland/meta-wayland-data-device.h"
 #include "wayland/meta-wayland-data-device-primary.h"
@@ -244,6 +245,18 @@ control_offer_receive (struct wl_client   *client,
       return;
     }
 
+  if (META_IS_SELECTION_SOURCE_WAYLAND (offer->owner))
+    {
+      MetaWaylandDataSource *source =
+        meta_selection_source_wayland_get_data_source (META_SELECTION_SOURCE_WAYLAND (offer->owner));
+
+      /* Hand the client's fd straight to the Wayland source, as wlroots
+       * does. Clipboard managers such as wl-clip-persist recognize their
+       * own selection by getting back the pipe they passed to receive. */
+      meta_wayland_data_source_send (source, mime_type, fd);
+      return;
+    }
+
   stream = g_unix_output_stream_new (fd, TRUE);
   meta_selection_transfer_async (selection,
                                  offer->selection_type,
